CHALLENGE 5: THE "SUPER" CONSTRUCTOR (Constructors in Inheritance)
================================================================================
Context: Ensuring data flows from Child to Parent correctly.
1. Base Class 'Employee': Has 'name' and 'id'. Constructor initializes both.
2. Subclass 'Developer': Adds 'programmingLanguage'.
3. The Goal: Use 'super(name, id)' in the Developer constructor to pass
   data up to the Employee class.
4. Requirement: Override 'toString()' in both to show the full data chain.
